The changes made include:

1. Added React.Suspense for handling the dynamic import
2. Implemented proper error handling with ErrorBoundary component
3. Used React.lazy for component importing with error catching
4. Added loading state while component is being loaded
5. Wrapped the component in proper div structure
6. Added error boundary to catch any rendering errors

This should handle the dynamic import issue and provide better error handling and user feedback. The ErrorBoundary will catch any rendering errors, and the Suspense component will handle the loading state while the component is being imported.

